Monitoring Strategy
Each workload application will be monitored to measure its impact on system resources using the following approach:
CPU-intensive (stress-ng)
Monitor using top, htop, and mpstat
Record peak CPU load and average load
Memory-intensive (memtester)
Monitor using free -h, vmstat, and smem
Record memory allocation, usage, and swap activity
Disk I/O (fio)
Monitor using iostat, df -h, and dstat
Record throughput, latency, and IOPS
Network-intensive (iperf3)
Monitor using iperf3 client-server measurements, ping, ss
Record latency, jitter, and throughput
Server workload (nginx)
Monitor using systemctl status nginx, top, netstat
Measure response time under simulated load
All monitoring commands will be executed via SSH, and results captured in tables and charts for performance analysis in Week 6.
